 "annotations": [
  {
   "id": "n-w-home",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-w-home",
   "text": "Home and its states, each at both widths on one row. The width holds the workings: the figure and its pace card left, the reason — where the money is, then every category worst-first — right, and reading one against the other is exactly what 360 cannot do. <b>The gauge lives at 360 only</b>, because <i>can I spend this, right now?</i> is asked in a shop with a phone in your hand; at a desk the question is whether you are on pace, and a dial has no memory of yesterday. Each state is its own row because each has its own fix."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-plan",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-plan",
   "text": "Where each naira gets its job, and the only screen whose <i>hero</i> is a figure nobody wants to be large: <b>unallocated</b>. It takes the top slot because it is the number that decides whether the plan is finished, and it is meant to reach ₦0.00 and disappear. Protection and rollover are their own columns at 1440 rather than marks on a row — both are decisions about a category, not decorations of it. The 360 row menu is the same two decisions on a screen with no room for columns."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-tx",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-tx",
   "text": "The list, and the two ways of having nothing in it. <b>A standing filter rail at 1440, tabs at 360</b>: stacked filters scroll the list away, and losing your place is the one thing that matters on this screen. <b>Both empty states are their own row</b> because they want opposite things — <i>nothing recorded</i> wants a movement, <i>filters match nothing</i> wants the filters cleared, and a single “no results” covering both is how a person clears their data looking for a button. Opening balances and debts are dated 24 September, the day before the cycle, so they never count as this cycle’s saving. <b>The bank-movements segment came off on 14 October</b> &mdash; ADR-013 defers the feature, and a segmented control with one segment is not a control. <b>The bank-movements segment came off on 14 October</b> &mdash; ADR-013 defers the feature, and a segmented control with one segment is not a control. <b>The bank-movements segment came off on 14 October</b> &mdash; ADR-013 defers the feature, and a segmented control with one segment is not a control. <b>The bank-movements segment came off on 14 October</b> &mdash; ADR-013 defers the feature, and a segmented control with one segment is not a control. <b>The bank-movements segment came off on 14 October</b> &mdash; ADR-013 defers the feature, and a segmented control with one segment is not a control. <b>The bank-movements segment came off on 14 October</b> &mdash; ADR-013 defers the feature, and a segmented control with one segment is not a control. <b>The bank-movements segment came off on 14 October</b> &mdash; ADR-013 defers the feature, and a segmented control with one segment is not a control. <b>The bank-movements segment came off on 14 October</b> &mdash; ADR-013 defers the feature, and a segmented control with one segment is not a control. <b>The bank-movements segment came off on 14 October</b> &mdash; ADR-013 defers the feature, and a segmented control with one segment is not a control."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-qa",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-qa",
   "text": "The persistent action, and <b>the reason the centre of the bottom bar is not a route</b>: story G2 wants a spend recorded while standing at a counter, so it is the largest target on the screen and it sits under the thumb. At 1440 it is a button in the header and a dialog, because a sheet sliding up a laptop is a phone gesture wearing a suit. <b>Delete is a quiet button, never a red one</b> — the same rule the primitives sheet sets, and the same one the category row follows."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-dg",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-dg",
   "text": "Both directions of money that is not this cycle’s: what you are saving for, and what is owed either way. <b>Debts loses its tabs entirely at 1440</b>, because the best thing width buys is sometimes one less control — the two lists sit side by side instead. At 360 they are tabs, and <i>Goals</i> is its own row here for that reason. <b>B. Colleague goes the other way</b>, and the direction is carried by the words <i>owes you</i> rather than by a sign or a colour. The printed record is on Foundations, not here: it leaves the app."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-mo",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-mo",
   "text": "Completed cycles, and the empty state that matters more than the populated one — a person meets this screen in month one, when there is nothing in it, and it has to say so without sounding broken. <b>A cycle is a salary month, 25th to 24th</b>, not a calendar month, which is the whole reason this screen exists under its own name rather than as “History”."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-zk",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-zk",
   "text": "The estimate and its workings, and <b>the workings are the point</b>: zakat is an obligation a person answers for, so every figure that goes into it is shown and named, and the nisab it is measured against is dated. <b>Nothing here advises.</b> The app reports what it can see and says plainly what it cannot — assets it does not hold, and the year it cannot witness. Sadaqah is a category of its own and is never counted as zakat."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-bank",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-bank",
   "text": "<b>Parked by ADR-013, and parked is not the same as wrong.</b> Bank movement is deferred until someone using the product asks for it and says they would pay &mdash; so these stay on the record as the design for it, and <b>none of them is to be built</b>. The paid-tier board that sat beside them (<i>09e</i>) is gone rather than parked: there is no tier any more, so it was not a deferred design but a wrong one. <i>17d &middot; cash in hand</i> is parked with them for a reason worth writing down &mdash; it looks like it stands alone, and it does not. Its whole job is to repair a mistake the bank feed introduces, by saying that a withdrawal is not a purchase. With nothing reading the bank, nobody is ever shown a withdrawal to classify: the ₦6,500 is recorded when it is spent, and D16 &mdash; cash left is income minus movements &mdash; is already right without it."
  }
 ]
}